From 44767ae72440e16eed4954a41edbd3d7334b6fd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:20:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/60] ppc32: restore the 32-bit PowerPC target configuration

V8 13.6 dropped the 32-bit PowerPC target altogether: v8config.h no longer
detects it, globals.h and every arch-dispatch site outside the backend test
V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 alone where 12.4 tested
V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC || V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64, and the ppc backend's ABI
macros test V8_HOST_ARCH_PPC64 alone where 12.4 tested
(V8_HOST_ARCH_PPC || V8_HOST_ARCH_PPC64) - which would turn
ABI_PASSES_HANDLES_IN_REGS on for a native 32-bit host.

This commit puts the configuration back exactly as 12.4 had it, site by
site (node/gnmirror-era census: 61 files outside the backend carry
PPC64-only guards at 13.6; the 36 that 12.4 expressed as "either PowerPC"
are restored here, the rest are genuinely 64-bit-only - ppc64 Linux
address hints, p10 code alignment, function descriptors, perf/gdb-jit -
or are rewritten by later patches of this series):

- include/v8config.h: V8_HOST_ARCH_PPC (__PPC__ / _ARCH_PPC, 32-bit host),
  V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC in the detection chain (_ARCH_PPC), 32-bit pointer
  size, big-endian (32-bit PowerPC is big-endian on every OS V8 has run
  on; 12.4's V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC_BE/LE macros are no longer consulted
  anywhere at 13.6).
- src/common/globals.h: USE_SIMULATOR for a non-PPC host, embedded
  constant pool on both widths (constant-pool.{h,cc} follow).
- the include dispatch chains (assembler/constants/register/reglist/
  macro-assembler/frame-constants/simulator/regexp/liftoff/unwinding-info
  arch headers, instruction-codes), register-configuration, reloc-info,
  interface descriptors, interpreter-assembler, debug-evaluate, code.cc,
  deserializer, runtime-atomics (the C++ SAB atomics the 32-bit port
  routes to), tick-sample, log.cc ("ppc"), liftoff-compiler,
  wasm-serialization, wasm-linkage, external-reference,
  v8-unwinder-state, compiler-specific.
- src/codegen/ppc/constants-ppc.h: the four ABI_* macros and
  ABI_USES_FUNCTION_DESCRIPTORS test both host widths again.

Everything a 12.4 series patch rewrites (c-linkage, code-generator's
trampoline scope, eh-frame, jump tables, embedded file writers,
liftoff-assembler-defs, wasm-objects, flag defaults, maglev's
CpuOperation answer, platform-posix) is left for that patch.
